{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), we have essentially no information about whether the image modality carries useful signal. The most impactful uncertainty is whether image features are informative at all, since a negative answer would eliminate ~36 multimodal configurations from further consideration. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the simplest possible image experiment—no aggregation, no fusion—so it cleanly isolates the information content of the image channel. Paired with the existing RNA baseline, it gives us two single-modality reference points, enabling us to interpret any future multimodal result as a measure of complementarity rather than conflating modality value with fusion/aggregation effects. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the current sparse evidence."
}

